00:56:48.370 --> 00:56:51.230
So I have used a commonly--

00:56:54.262 --> 00:56:56.920
I can't name names, but
a commonly used data

00:56:56.920 --> 00:57:03.315
visualization tool, which
is kind of a click and drag

00:57:03.315 --> 00:57:03.940
and everything.

00:57:03.940 --> 00:57:05.050
And I just don't find it--

00:57:05.050 --> 00:57:08.740
I like to know what's
going on behind the scenes.

00:57:08.740 --> 00:57:10.570
And when I'm writing
in Shiny code,

00:57:10.570 --> 00:57:12.490
I know how things fit together.

00:57:12.490 --> 00:57:14.740
But when I'm doing-- if I
was focusing more in Tableau

00:57:14.740 --> 00:57:19.345
or another tool, I wouldn't--
any of those visualizations

00:57:19.345 --> 00:57:21.970
that can be done in Tableau, but
I wouldn't have the same sense

00:57:21.970 --> 00:57:22.780
of control.

00:57:22.780 --> 00:57:24.430
So that's my
personal preference,

00:57:24.430 --> 00:57:28.720
and I'm not saying
